# No git commits (agent policy)

**Kevin commits. Agents do not.**

## Never do

- Run `git commit`, `git commit --amend`, or any other command that creates or rewrites commits.
- Stage files **for the purpose of committing** unless Kevin explicitly asks you to stage (rare).
- Ask “Want me to commit?” or “Should I commit with this message?” — not even after drafting a message.
- Offer to commit as a follow-up or sign-off.

## Do instead

- Implement, verify, and summarize changes.
- When helpful, **draft a commit message** in chat if Kevin asks — or briefly note that changes are ready to commit. Stop there.
- Kevin runs `git add` and `git commit` locally.

## Related

- Agents **never push** (see `jira-ticket-and-branch.mdc`).
- Jira ticket + feature branch rules still apply before implementation.
